### Mundo Invest - Cenários de Falhas
### Requisições para testar tratamento de erros e casos excepcionais

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

###############################################################################
### FALHAS - Processamento de Webhooks
###############################################################################

### 1. Processar webhook duplicado (idempotência - mesmo event_id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_123",
  "card_id": "card_456",
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T12:00:00Z"
}

### 2. Processar webhook com cliente não encontrado
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_999",
  "card_id": "card_999",
  "cliente_email": "nao.existe@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T15:00:00Z"
}

### 3. Processar webhook com cliente não encontrado (email inexistente)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_1000",
  "card_id": "card_1000",
  "cliente_email": "cliente.inexistente@dominio-fake.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T17:00:00Z"
}

###############################################################################
### FALHAS - Erros de Serviço Externo
###############################################################################

### 4. Processar webhook quando serviço Pipefy está indisponível
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_2000",
  "card_id": "card_2000",
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T18:00:00Z"
}

### 5. Processar webhook com card_id inválido (não existe no Pipefy)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_2001",
  "card_id": "card_invalido_999999",
  "cliente_email": "maria.santos@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T19:00:00Z"
}

###############################################################################
### FALHAS - Concorrência e Race Conditions
###############################################################################

### 6. Processar webhook simultâneo para mesmo cliente (simular concorrência)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_3000",
  "card_id": "card_3000",
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T20:00:00Z"
}

### 7. Processar webhook com timestamp futuro (data inválida)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_3001",
  "card_id": "card_3001",
  "cliente_email": "maria.santos@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2099-12-31T23:59:59Z"
}

### 8. Processar webhook com timestamp muito antigo (data passada)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_3002",
  "card_id": "card_3002",
  "cliente_email": "pedro.oliveira@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

###############################################################################
### FALHAS - Erros de Sistema
###############################################################################

### 9. Processar webhook com payload JSON malformado (adicione caractere inválido no final)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_4000",
  "card_id": "card_4000",
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T21:00:00Z"
}

### 10. Processar webhook com campos extras não esperados
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_4001",
  "card_id": "card_4001",
  "cliente_email": "maria.santos@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T22:00:00Z",
  "campo_extra": "valor_nao_esperado",
  "outro_campo": 12345
}

### 11. Processar webhook com tipos de dados incorretos
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": 123456,
  "card_id": 789012,
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T23:00:00Z"
}

###############################################################################
### FALHAS - Criação de Clientes
###############################################################################

### 12. Criar cliente com email duplicado (deve falhar se já existe)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "João Silva",
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Atualização cadastral",
  "valor_patrimonio": 250000
}

### 13. Criar cliente com tipo_solicitacao inválido
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "Teste Tipo Invalido",
  "cliente_email": "teste.tipo.invalido@example.com",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Tipo que não existe",
  "valor_patrimonio": 100000
}

### 14. Criar cliente com caracteres especiais no nome
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "Teste <script>alert('xss')</script>",
  "cliente_email": "teste.xss@example.com",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Atualização cadastral",
  "valor_patrimonio": 100000
}

### 15. Criar cliente com nome muito longo (overflow)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "Nome Muito Longo Que Excede O Limite Permitido Pelo Sistema E Deve Causar Um Erro De Validacao Por Exceder O Tamanho Maximo Do Campo",
  "cliente_email": "teste.longo@example.com",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Abertura de conta",
  "valor_patrimonio": 100000
}

###############################################################################
### FALHAS - Endpoints Inexistentes
###############################################################################

### 16. Acessar endpoint inexistente
GET {{baseUrl}}/endpoint-inexistente

### 17. Acessar endpoint com método HTTP incorreto
GET {{baseUrl}}/clientes

### 18. Acessar endpoint com método HTTP incorreto
PUT {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated

###############################################################################
### INSTRUÇÕES DE USO
###############################################################################
# 
# Este arquivo contém cenários de falhas para testar:
# - Idempotência (webhooks duplicados)
# - Clientes não encontrados
# - Erros de serviços externos (Pipefy)
# - Concorrência e race conditions
# - Timestamps inválidos (futuro, passado)
# - Payloads malformados
# - Campos extras não esperados
# - Tipos de dados incorretos
# - Emails duplicados
# - Tipos de solicitação inválidos
# - Caracteres especiais (XSS)
# - Overflow de campos
# - Endpoints inexistentes
# - Métodos HTTP incorretos
#
# Todas as requisições devem retornar erro (4xx ou 5xx)
#
###############################################################################
